{"parentUuid":"7f24327d-98d4-4e49-9771-13dd3ba220ae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"gen_01M1016R5T2QYHX7W03M4VPSAJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The product page title now appears immediately on navigation.\n\n**The problem:** `app/product/page.tsx` awaited `getInventory()` at the top of the page component, and that function calls `connection()` (in `lib/data.ts:4`), which forces the data to be fetched at request time. Because the await sat above everything in the page, the entire page — including the completely static \"Premium Widget\" heading — was blocked behind that request-time work. With `cacheComponents: true` enabled, Next.js couldn't prerender any shell for the route, so navigating from home meant waiting for the server before anything rendered.\n\n**The fix:** I moved the inventory fetch into a small async `Inventory` component and wrapped it in a `<Suspense>` boundary with a \"Loading inventory…\" fallback. The `<h1>` now lives outside the dynamic boundary, so it's part of the prerendered static shell that `<Link>` can prefetch and show instantly; the stock count and price stream in when the server responds.\n\nThe build confirms it: `/product` now shows as `◐ (Partial Prerender)` — static HTML with dynamic server-streamed content — instead of being fully request-blocked."}],"model":"claude-fable-5","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5844,"cache_read_input_tokens":28409,"output_tokens":449,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5844},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"3e4647ec-8e8d-4175-9a9c-e4e93e18f0eb","timestamp":"2026-08-26T21:56:54.795Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"s